       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as 850 mg three times daily, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Possible intended doses include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for IR.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If you do mean 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional."
