      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The current FDA label doesn't support the claim that this dose is within the maximum. The label's maximum for metformin IR is 2,550 mg/day, and for ER it is 2,000 mg/day. Metformin 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, about twice the labeled maximum. Because it is a clear overdose, I can't enter it as written, even with your confirmation.\n\nIf you want this order in the system, here are some options:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total,** for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **A different dose you specify** that stays within labeled limits.\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason to go above the labeled maximum, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. They can approve it through the hospital's override process. I can enter any of the options above right away."
